  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider the following molecules and statements related to them:</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0173_cbab8078aa9b.png\" style=\"width: 472px; height: 140px;\" /></p><p>(a) (B) is more likely to be crystaline than (A)</p><p>(b) (B) has higher boiling point than (A)</p><p>(c) (B) dissolves more readily than (A) in water</p><p>Identify the correct option from below:</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "(a) and (b) are true",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "(a) and (c) are true",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "only (a) is true",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "(b) and (c) are true",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The molecules of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;are joined by intermolecular hydrogen bonding and molecules of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> associated through dipole-dipole interactions.Hence, the B is more likely to be crystalline than A. Due to inter molecular<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>-</mo></math>Bonding in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>, than&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;is more soluble and having more boiling&nbsp;point than&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.</p><p><strong>*Note: All the three&nbsp;statements given in the question are correct but the given answer according to NTA,&nbsp;is statements (b) and (c).</strong></p>"
  }
}